---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/PageHero.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CTASection from '@/components/CTASection.astro';

const varieties = [
  {
    name: 'Red Apple Varieties',
    description:
      'Iranian red apples are known for their color, crunch and versatile sizing — a dependable category for wholesale programs.',
    href: '/red-apple-export/',
    color: 'bg-apple-500',
  },
  {
    name: 'Golden Apple Varieties',
    description:
      'Golden apples offer a sweet, balanced flavor and attractive pale color favored across regional markets.',
    href: '/golden-apple-export/',
    color: 'bg-gold-400',
  },
  {
    name: 'Green Apple Varieties',
    description:
      'Green apples bring tangy acidity and firm texture, well suited to buyers seeking a tart profile.',
    href: '/green-apple-export/',
    color: 'bg-forest-500',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Iranian Apple Varieties — Red, Golden & Green Types | SibExport"
  description="A buyer's guide to Iranian apple varieties: red, golden and green apple classes from Iran's orchards, with commercial notes for importers and wholesale buyers."
  path="/iranian-apple-varieties/"
  ogImage="/images/varieties.png"
>
  <Breadcrumbs
    items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Iranian Apple Varieties' }]}
  />
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Our Products"
    title="Iranian apple varieties"
    description="Iran is one of the world's major apple producers. Here is what international buyers should know about the varieties and categories its orchards supply."
  />

  <article class="container-site py-14 lg:py-20">
    <div class="prose-site mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <h2>Iran's apple landscape, briefly</h2>
      <p>
        Iran ranks among the largest apple-producing countries in the world,
        with an annual crop measured in millions of tonnes. The heart of that
        production lies in the northwest: the provinces of West and East
        Azerbaijan, where elevations, cold winters and long autumn days
        produce apples with dense flesh, developed sugars and the firmness
        export buyers require. Urmia, in West Azerbaijan, sits at the center
        of this region and is widely regarded as one of Iran's most important
        apple cities.
      </p>
      <p>
        For an international buyer, this matters for one practical reason:
        <strong>origin concentration</strong>. Because so much of Iran's apple
        crop grows within a compact, well-connected region, a supplier based
        there can genuinely follow fruit from orchard to loading — an
        advantage fragmented growing regions cannot always offer.
      </p>

      <h2>The three commercial color classes</h2>
      <p>
        International apple trade is organized less around botanical variety
        names and more around commercial categories. In wholesale practice,
        Iranian apples divide into three classes, each with its own buyer
        profile and handling requirements.
      </p>
      <p>
        The classification below describes the commercial categories
        SibExport works with. Within each, the exact varieties we can supply
        in a given season are confirmed per order — availability genuinely
        changes with harvest and storage cycles, and we prefer written
        confirmation over brochure promises.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto mt-10 grid max-w-3xl gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
      {
        varieties.map((v) => (
          <a
            href={v.href}
            class="group rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-sm transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-md"
          >
            <span class={`block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full ${v.color}`} aria-hidden="true" />
            <h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold">{v.name}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
              {v.description}
            </p>
            <span class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm font-semibold text-forest-700">
              View details
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="transition-transform duration-200 group-hover:translate-x-1" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14" /><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7" /></svg>
            </span>
          </a>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <div class="prose-site mx-auto mt-12 max-w-3xl">
      <h2>Red apples: the volume leader</h2>
      <p>
        Red apples are Iran's signature export category. Grown across the
        northwest's orchards, Iranian red apples combine strong color
        development with firm flesh and a balanced sweet-tart profile. They
        are versatile in trade: the same category serves retail chain
        programs, wholesale market stalls and repackers. Buyers typically
        specify them by count per carton and color grade, with mid-size,
        well-colored fruit the most demanded profile.
      </p>
      <p>
        Commercial detail on this category lives on the
        <a href="/red-apple-export/">red apple export</a> page.
      </p>

      <h2>Golden apples: the sweet favorite</h2>
      <p>
        The golden category — commercially associated with Golden Delicious
        and similar types — offers pale gold skin, crisp white flesh and a
        distinctly sweet, low-acid eating experience. Golden apples are a
        familiar staple across regional markets and are commonly bought
        alongside red fruit in mixed programs. Their thinner skin demands
        more careful handling than red categories, which makes harvest care
        and interior packing the decisive quality factors.
      </p>
      <p>
        Commercial detail on this category lives on the
        <a href="/golden-apple-export/">golden apple export</a> page.
      </p>

      <h2>Green apples: the tart complement</h2>
      <p>
        Green apples supply what the other categories cannot: acidity. Firm,
        tart and visually distinctive, they round out a three-color program
        and hold a loyal customer base in many markets. Their firmness makes
        them robust travelers, well suited to demanding distribution chains
        and longer transit.
      </p>
      <p>
        Commercial detail on this category lives on the
        <a href="/green-apple-export/">green apple supply</a> page.
      </p>

      <h2>Seasonality: when Iranian apples are available</h2>

<figure class="my-8">
      <img
        src="/images/banner-season.svg"
        alt="Iranian apple harvest and storage seasons"
        width="1200"
        height="480"
        loading="lazy"
        class="w-full rounded-xl border border-border shadow-sm"
      />
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-center text-xs text-muted-foreground">Iranian apple harvest and storage seasons</figcaption>
    </figure>
      <p>
        Iran's apple harvest typically begins in late summer and runs through
        autumn, with the exact window shifting by region, elevation and
        variety. Once harvested, fruit destined for later shipments moves
        into cold storage, which extends commercial availability for much of
        the year. In practice, this means buyers can usually plan programs
        across several seasons of demand — fresh-harvest fruit in autumn,
        storage fruit through winter and spring.
      </p>
      <p>
        What we will not do is quote fixed availability months ahead of
        reality. Seasonal planning works best as a conversation: tell us your
        market's demand pattern, and we will map it honestly against the
        Iranian crop calendar.
      </p>

      <h2>General information versus confirmed supply</h2>
      <p>
        One distinction recurs throughout this page because it protects
        buyers: <strong>the general characteristics of Iranian apple
        varieties are widely known; the specific varieties, sizes and grades
        SibExport can confirm for your order are a commercial fact that
        depends on the season.</strong> We keep the two separate on purpose.
        Everything on this page is honest orientation; everything in your
        quotation is a written commitment. That is how a repeatable supply
        relationship is built.
      </p>

      <h2>Choosing the right category for your market</h2>
      <p>
        Buyers new to Iranian supply often ask which category to start with.
        The honest answer depends on your customers: red apples are the
        broadest, safest volume category; golden apples add a sweet profile
        with strong regional recognition; green apples differentiate a range
        and serve tart-apple demand. Many buyers begin with a single mixed
        container to test market response before committing to a seasonal
        program.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are planning a first order, our
        <a href="/apple-export-process/">export process</a> page shows exactly
        how an inquiry becomes a delivered shipment — and the
        <a href="/request-a-quotation/">quotation form</a> is the fastest way
        to start.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <CTASection
    title="Not sure which variety fits your market?"
    description="Tell us your market and customers — we will recommend the category and configuration that fits, honestly."
  />
</BaseLayout>
